At Wed, 25 May 2005 09:44:24 +0200,
Lorenzo Milesi wrote:
> 
> hi
> 
> A friend of mine has just bought a brand new Asus laptop, equiped with
> an Intel 82801fb.
> We're having lots of troubles with this card, and still we couldn't
> get it working. We previously tried with azm module and then with alsa
> 1.0.9's hda driver. both modules load correctly, alsamixer works, but
> absolutely no sound comes out from the speakers.
> I was missing one thing: when loading the hda module it says:
> hda_codec.c:512:
> hda_codec.c: no AFG node found

This message is mostly harmless.  The driver detected the modem codec
in the tree, which isn't supported yet.  In the latest version, this
message is suppressed.  The serious message is "no codecs
initialized".  If this message appears, the driver won't work at all.

If the driver is loaded and doesn't complain like above, the silent
problem is likely the wrong PIN assignment.
For ALC880 codec (you can check it in /proc/asound/card0/codec#*
file), try a different "model" module option.  See
ALSA-Configuration.txt for details.  Make sure that you use the 
latest 1.0.9rc4!

If none of models matches your device, try to build drivers with debug
option and set model=test.  This will enable almost all available
controls for testing.  Check different PIN configurations via
alsamixer, and report it to here together with the content of
/proc/asound/card0/codec#* files.


